<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_3_5_2" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_3_5_2" name="3.5.2 Assign equipment and vehicles to crews" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>The only modelled process in group 3.5. The other four - crew definition, the district map and the availability watch - are standing capabilities with no instance boundary and are specified rather than drawn. Assignment of a pool item to a crew is a repeating path and does have an instance, which is the distinction the notation rule turns on.</documentation>
    <startEvent id="n_352_start" name="A crew needs its assignment, or an assignment has changed"><messageEventDefinition id="n_352_start_md"/></startEvent>
    <serviceTask id="n_352_need" name="Take the crew definition and the equipment it needs"><documentation>3.5.2. From the standing crew definition at 3.5.1.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_352_pool" name="Read the available vehicle and tool pool"><documentation>3.5.2. Hooks to 13.3 Manage mobile and vehicle inventory.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_352_gate" name="Availability"/>
    <serviceTask id="n_352_ded" name="Assign a dedicated vehicle"><documentation>3.5.2 variant.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_352_shared" name="Assign from the shared pool"><documentation>3.5.2 variant. A shared assignment carries a period, or two crews plan against the same vehicle.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_352_spec" name="Issue a specialist tool per job"><documentation>3.5.2 variant. Issued against the job rather than the crew, so it returns.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_352_rec" name="Record the assignment against the crew"><documentation>3.5.2.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_352_down" name="Mark equipment down or shared"><documentation>3.5.2. Equipment marked down feeds 3.5.4, which feeds 3.4.4 when a placement is already in force.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_352_pub" name="Publish the crew's capability to scheduling"><documentation>3.5.2. A crew without its equipment is not the crew the schedule matched on.</documentation></sendTask>
    <endEvent id="n_352_end" name="Crew equipped and publishable"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_start_n_352_need" sourceRef="n_352_start" targetRef="n_352_need" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_need_n_352_pool" sourceRef="n_352_need" targetRef="n_352_pool" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_pool_n_352_gate" sourceRef="n_352_pool" targetRef="n_352_gate" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_gate_n_352_ded" sourceRef="n_352_gate" targetRef="n_352_ded" name="dedicated vehicle available"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[assignmentMode = "dedicated"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_gate_n_352_spec" sourceRef="n_352_gate" targetRef="n_352_spec" name="specialist tool required"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[assignmentMode = "specialistPerJob"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_gate_n_352_shared" sourceRef="n_352_gate" targetRef="n_352_shared" name="from the shared pool"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_ded_n_352_rec" sourceRef="n_352_ded" targetRef="n_352_rec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_shared_n_352_rec" sourceRef="n_352_shared" targetRef="n_352_rec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_spec_n_352_rec" sourceRef="n_352_spec" targetRef="n_352_rec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_rec_n_352_down" sourceRef="n_352_rec" targetRef="n_352_down" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_down_n_352_pub" sourceRef="n_352_down" targetRef="n_352_pub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_352_pub_n_352_end" sourceRef="n_352_pub" targetRef="n_352_end" name=""/>
  </process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="dg_P_3_5_2">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="pl_P_3_5_2" bpmnElement="P_3_5_2">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="sh_n_352_start" bpmnElement="n_352_start"><dc:Bounds x="132" y="217" width="36" height="36"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
